      "message": "Hi, this is the usb charger shared thread patch. Implemented as an option right now, few boards have code that operate on tasks directly but if this works I think we can sort that out and drop the per-port thread code from Zephyr, and this can be used on legacy code as well. Made this work by refactoring the drivers into a init+loop function and then having a usb charger atomic variable for the event bits, reusing the task one to flag what port have been signaled (see the two previous patches).\n\nLet me know what you think.",
